  "lesson": "## Trade hits between two decks\n\nHot cues A1, A2, B1 and B2 on hits from two different tracks. Every beat, press the next cue and snap the crossfader to that deck: A on the one, B on the two, A on the three, B on the four, with a pickup on the and-of-eight. Two bars per sequence, four times.\n\nThis is the two-deck reduction of DJ TechTools' four-song juggle: the crossfader routes the hit, the cue plays it, and both must land together or the wrong track is heard. Left hand on the pads of A, right hand on B and the crossfader between them; the crossfader moves on every press.\n",
  "skills": [
    "cue-juggling",
    "crossfader-cut"
  ],
  "genre": [
    "hip-hop",
    "open-format"
  ],
  "path": "combined",
  "level": 3,
  "sources": [
